    "name": "@BET_THM",
    "url": "%40BET_THM",
    "documentation": "$$$$ @BET_THM NOTICE  FD218221  26/02/13    21:15:07     12462          \n                                             DATE     26/02/13\n\n    Procedure @BET_THM                     Voir aussi : @SATURA\n    ------------------  \n    MAT1 SEC1 = @BET_THM MOD1 CHPO1 ;\n\n\n    Subject:\n    -------\n\n       The @BET_THM procedure constructs the MAT1 characteristic field\n    associated with the MOD1 model in the case of a THERMOHYDRIQUE formulation,\n    using the BETON_THM's law, as well as the second member of the system of\n    coupled equations associated with this model. This procedure replaces the\n    MATE operator in the case of a THERMOHYDRIQUE formulation.\n\n       It calls on the @SATURA procedure, which gives the saturation\n    of the porous medium with liquid water. More generally, this procedure\n    contains the material characteristics of the different phases constituting\n    the medium: porous solid (concrete), liquid water and steam, dry air.\n    A priori, only the characteristics of the solid phase are likely to be modified.\n\n    Comment:\n    --------\n\n    MOD1   = MMODEL, model THERMOHYDRIQUE BETON_THM;\n    CHPO1  = CHPOINT of primary unknowns (PG, PC, T);\n\n    MAT1   = MCHAML of characteristics associated with MOD1;\n    SEC1   = CHPOINT to be added to the second member during resolution\n             (preset in PASAPAS);\n\n    Note:\n    -----\n\n       The model THERMOHYDRIQUE BETON_THM describes the thermohydric behavior\n    of a porous, deformable, unsaturated medium, valid for studying early age,\n    aging (drying), and high-temperature behavior, according to the approach\n    developed by G. Sciume and S. Dal Pont [1] [2].\n\n    References :\n    ------------\n\n    [1] A multiphysics model for concrete at early age applied to repairs problems\n        G. Sciume, F. Benboudjema, C. de Sa, F. Pesavento, Y. Berthaud, B.A. Schrefler\n        Engineering Structures, 2013, 57, pp.374-387.\n        https://doi.org/10.1016/j.engstruct.2013.09.042\n\n    [2] A multiphase thermo-hydro-mechanical model for concrete at high temperatures\n        Finite element implementation and validation under LOCA load\n        S. Dal Pont, S. Durand b, B.A. Schrefler\n        Nuclear Engineering and Design, 2007, 237(22), pp.2137-2150\n        https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nucengdes.2007.03.047\n\n    [3] Thermo-hygro-chemical model of concrete: from curing to high temperature behavior\n        G. Sciume, M. Henrique Moreira, S. Dal Pont\n        Materials and structures, 2024, 57(8), pp.186\n        https://doi.org/10.1617/s11527-024-02454-3\n\n$$$$\n \n"
