    "url": "CCON",
    "documentation": "$$$$ CCON     NOTICE  JC220346  16/11/18    21:15:26     9187           \n                                             DATE     16/11/18\n\n    Operateur CCON                                Voir aussi : PART\n    --------------  \n    TAB1 = CCON ( | 'STR1' | ) MAIL1 ;\n                  | 'STR2' | \n\n\n    +-----------------------------------------------------------------+\n    | THIS OPERATOR IS OBSOLETE AND WILL BE REMOVED IN THE NEXT       |\n    | FUTURE                                                          |\n    |                                                                 |\n    | ITS FUNCTIONALITIES HAVE BEEN INCLUDED IN THE MORE GENERAL PART |\n    | OPERATOR                                                   ==== |\n    +-----------------------------------------------------------------+\n\n    \n    Description :\n    -------------\n\n    The CCON operator separates the connected components of a mesh\n    and stores them in a TABLE object indexed by integers 1, 2, 3...\n    \n    When the 'STR1' keyword is present (case of lines), the nodes \n    belonging to more than two elements separate the connected\n    components.\n\n    When the 'STR2' keyword is present (case of surfaces), neighbours\n    are connected through the vertices, and only if these belong to no\n    more than two elements.\n\n \n \n \n"
