    "name": "COUT",
    "url": "COUT",
    "documentation": "$$$$ COUT     NOTICE  GOUNAND   21/03/31    21:15:00     10931          \n                                             DATE     21/03/31\n                                             \n  Operateur COUTURE                       Voir aussi :\n     -----------------  \n    ---------------------  \n    ---------------------\n\n     SURF1 =  COUT LIG1 LIG2  ;\n\n     Description :\n     _____________\n\n     The COUTURE operator constructs a surface which connects two \n     lines by means of triangles.\n\n     Contents :\n     __________\n\n     LIG1  | : lines between which the surface is generated\n     LIG2  |   (MAILLAGE type)\n \n     SURF1   : created surface (MAILLAGE type)\n\n     Note :\n     ________\n\n     Both lines should have the same orientation.\n\n\n    ---------------------\n    |  2nd possibility  |\n    ---------------------\n\n     MAIL2 =  COUT MAIL1 POIN1 ;\n\n     Description :\n     _____________\n\n     The COUTURE operator constructs a mesh which connects a mesh and\n     a point (star operator).\n\n     Contents :\n     __________\n\n     POIN1   : point (POINT type) to be connected to mesh MAIL1\n     MAIL1   : mesh (MAILLAGE type) made of POI1, SEG2, TRI3 or QUA4\n               elements\n\n     MAIL2   : output mesh (MAILLAGE type) made of SEG2, TRI3, TET4 or\n               PYR5 elements\n\n     Note :\n     ________\n\n     POIN1 can be part of MAIL1. In this case, the elements of MAIL1\n     connected to POIN1 are not starred.\n \n"
