    "name": "DEBM",
    "url": "DEBM",
    "documentation": "$$$$ DEBM     NOTICE  CHAT      11/09/12    21:15:45     7124           \n                                             DATE     11/09/12\n\n    Operateur DEBMETH                        Voir aussi : FINM ARGU\n    -----------------                                     RESP  QUIT  \n    DEBMETH   METH1 (OBJ1?TYP1  OBJ2?TYP2  .... ) ;\n\n\n    Description :\n    -----------\n    The scope is to define a method which can be applied on an object\nof type OBJET.\n\n    The DEBMETH operator creates a PROCEDUR type object which\n is composed of a set of elementary instructions : the first\n instruction is DEBMETH (beginning of method) and the last is\n FINMETH (end of method).\n\n    Comments :\n    ----------\n\n  This operator is strictly issued from the DEBPROC operator. The\ndifference can be seen only while executing the issued procedure which\ncan be applied only on an object of type OBJET.\n \n \n"
