    "documentation": "$$$$ DIAD     NOTICE  CHAT      11/09/12    21:15:53     7124           \n                                             DATE     11/09/12\n\n    Operateur DIAD                           Voir aussi : MULTIDEC\n    --------------                                        MULTIREC  \n    LIST1  = DIAD (MOT1) LIST2  ;\n                                     MOT1='DIRE','INVE','IVIN'\n\n\n    Description :\n    -------------\n\n    If MOT1='DIRE'(ct), the DIAD operator constructs LIST1,\n    suppressing one value of LIST2 out of two (LISTREEL type).\n    The first point is always maintained.\n\n    If MOT1='INVE'(rse), the DIAD operator constructs LIST1 by\n    inserting a zero between each point of LIST2, after the first \n    point and length(LIST1)=2*length(LIST2) if length (LIST2)\n    is even, or 2*length(LIST2)-1 if length(LIST2) is odd.\n\n    If MOT1='IVIN', the DIAD operator constructs LIST1 by inserting \n    the mean of the two bordering points according to the same \n    length rules as above.\n\n     \n    options :\n    ---------\n\n    MOT1 equals 'DIRE', 'INVE' or 'IVIN'. The default is 'DIRE'.\n\n\n \n"
