    "documentation": "$$$$ FORBLOC  NOTICE  CHAT      11/09/12    21:16:17     7124           \n                                             DATE     11/09/12\n\n  Procedure FORBLOC                    Voir aussi :\n        -----------------  \n        CHP2 CHP3 = FORBLOC GEO1 CHP1 FLOT1 ( LOG1 )\n        \n\n\n\n        Description :\n        -------------\n        In 2d potential vector magnetostatics, it enables the\n        calculation of forces on an inductor by means of a surface \n        integral  J * B\n\n\n        Contents :\n        ---------- \n\n        GEO1     mesh    \n        CHP1     potential defined at least on GEO1\n        FLOT1    electric current density on GEO1 \n        LOG1    optional  logical VRAI for axisymmetric problems\n           ( default  plane problem )\n        Output data :\n\n        CHP2 = CHPOINT of forces at the nodes ( FX FY ) (in\n               axisymmetry, they are called FX and FY all the same)\n          ( result by unit length for plane problems and by radian\n           for axisymmetric problems)\n        CHP3   CHPOINT of the resultant at the barycentre of GEO1 \n\n\n \n \n"
