    "documentation": "$$$$ NORMALIM NOTICE  MB234859  17/10/02    21:15:19     9577           \n                                             DATE     17/10/02\n\n  Procedure NORMALIM                       Voir aussi :\n    ------------------  \n    LREEL1 EVOL1 = NORMALIM EVOL2 (FLOT1)\n\n\n    Description :\n    -------------\n\n    The NORMALIM procedure makes it possible to generate the \n    normed functions EVOL1 (including N curves) associated with\n    EVOL2 (including N curves). LREEL1 (including N FLOTTANT)\n    contains the norm of each curve of EVOL1.\n\n    Options :\n    ---------\n\n    The default norm input is the norm L2 estimated by means\n    of the SOMM operator. If the FLOTTANT FLOT1 is input, it means\n    that the analysis carried out is a wavelet analysis, and that\n    the norm is defined in relation to a sampling of period FLOT1.\n\n\n \n \n"
