    "documentation": "$$$$ PAS_DEFA NOTICE  PASCAL    20/12/03    21:15:05     10801          \n                                             DATE     20/12/03\n\n\n    procedure PAS_DEFA   \n    ------------------\n\n\n\n    This procedure is invoked at the beginning of PASAPAS. It permits\n    to set default values and it create the working table WTAB used\n    in pasapas.\n\n    Syntax :\n    --------\n \n    PAS_DEFA TAB1 ;\n\n    With TAB1, the input data table of the PASAPAS procedure.\n\n    In output, PAS_DEFA returns TAB1 with a new indice WTABLE.\n\n    ... \n\n    'CHAR_MODE'       : LOGIQUE, true if there is a CHARGEMENT named MODE\n\n    'CHAR_MATE'       : LOGIQUE, true if there is a CHARGEMENT named MATE\n\n    'CHAR_BLOD'       : LOGIQUE, true if there is a CHARGEMENT named BLOD\n\n    'CHAR_BLOM'       : LOGIQUE, true if there is a CHARGEMENT named BLOM\n\n    'CHAR_BLOT'       : LOGIQUE, true if there is a CHARGEMENT named BLOT\n\n    ... \n\n$$$$\n\n    \n \n \n \n"
